RudeSocket NEWS - User visible changes.
See ChangeLog for more detailed information on internal changes
See the end for copying conditions.

_______________________________________________________________________________
Release 1.3.0 - Matthew Flood 2026-07-30

	- BEHAVIOR CHANGE: connectSSL() now verifies the server's certificate
	  by default (system CA store + hostname check) and fails otherwise.
	  Call the new Socket::setSSLVerify(false) to accept self-signed or
	  mismatched certificates.
	- TLS repair: send SNI (modern servers rejected the handshake without
	  it), use the OpenSSL >= 1.1 API (TLS_client_method), consult
	  SSL_pending() so readline() over SSL no longer deadlocks, honor
	  setTimeout() on SSL reads and sends, and report SSL errors through
	  getError() instead of printing to stderr.
	- New CMake build system (autotools files retained but deprecated);
	  installs CMake package config and pkg-config files. SSL support is
	  optional: -DRUDESOCKET_WITH_SSL=OFF builds without OpenSSL, and
	  connectSSL() then fails gracefully with a clear error message
	  (previously it silently fell back to an UNENCRYPTED connection).
	- Code modernized to compile cleanly as C++17 with -Wall -Wextra
	  (sprintf -> snprintf, unused parameters, Windows header ordering).
	- Added test suite (ctest: echo, timeout, and SSL tests against a
	  local openssl s_server) and GitHub Actions CI covering Linux
	  x86_64/ARM, macOS, and Windows, plus an ASan/UBSan job.
	- New README with verified quick-start examples.

